
According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Medical Device Testing and Validation Service market was valued at USD 7,499 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 11,664 million by 2034, growing at a steady CAGR of 6.8% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is propelled by increasing regulatory scrutiny worldwide, the accelerating pace of digital‑health innovation, and the rising tendency of manufacturers to outsource specialized validation work.
What is Medical Device Testing and Validation Service?
Medical device testing and validation services refer to the suite of third‑party or in‑house technical and regulatory activities that confirm a device’s safety, performance, quality and compliance. The scope covers laboratory testing, engineering analysis, clinical evaluation and full documentation in line with standards such as FDA regulations, ISO 13485 and the EU MDR before commercialization. By delivering objective, auditable evidence, these services enable manufacturers to satisfy regulators, investors and end‑users.
